      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "intro",
          "type": "md",
          "x": -338.46570509958406,
          "y": -187.94876133587596,
          "z": 14,
          "w": 340,
          "text": "# Askeroo\n\nA modern CLI prompt library that treats a terminal flow like a real, navigable form.\n\n[TypeScript] [React] [Ink]"
        },
        {
          "id": "stack",
          "type": "md",
          "x": 1767.8404819973373,
          "y": 61.24963712223894,
          "z": 2,
          "w": 300,
          "text": "The first stateful CLI that allows back navigation. I created Askeroo after wishing more from the available prompt wizards that were avaiable. I wanted something modular and configurable for different needs."
        },
        {
          "id": "note-0",
          "type": "sticky",
          "x": 1120.7275158404896,
          "y": -116.07767887803142,
          "z": 3,
          "color": "yellow",
          "text": "Stateful back-navigation — revise earlier answers at any time"
        },
        {
          "id": "note-1",
          "type": "sticky",
          "x": 1147.7977633982673,
          "y": 122.57442147986589,
          "z": 4,
          "color": "blue",
          "text": "Conditional fields that respond to prior input"
        },
        {
          "id": "note-2",
          "type": "sticky",
          "x": 1149.2121827001579,
          "y": 345.47149769696455,
          "z": 5,
          "color": "green",
          "text": "Built-in task runners for long-running steps"
        },
        {
          "id": "n4-code",
          "type": "code",
          "x": 182.33251760807434,
          "y": 506.1504133331703,
          "z": 8,
          "w": 420,
          "text": "// Your flow function runs multiple times\nconst flow = async () => {\n  const role = await radio({\n      label: \"Select your role\",\n      options: [\"Developer\", \"Designer\"],\n  });\n\n  if (role === \"Developer\") {\n    const language = await radio({\n        label: \"Preferred language\",\n        options: [\"TypeScript\", \"JavaScript\"],\n    });\n    return { role, language };\n  }\n\n  const tool = await radio({\n      label: \"Design tool\",\n      options: [\"Figma\", \"Sketch\"],\n  });\n  return { role, tool };\n};",
          "lang": "js"
        },
        {
          "id": "n6-md",
          "type": "md",
          "x": 488.12200650666955,
          "y": 934.0370813787082,
          "z": 10,
          "w": 340,
          "text": "## Testing\n\nYou can make prompts conditional by guarding them with conditions. In this example, the \"Preferred language\" prompt will only get shown if the \"Developer\" role is chosen."
        },
        {
          "id": "n7-code",
          "type": "code",
          "x": -542.9636050799502,
          "y": 494.79339111111966,
          "z": 11,
          "w": 420,
          "text": "const flow = async () => {\n  const name = await text({\n      message: \"Name\",\n  });\n  return { name };\n}\n\nconst result = await ask(flow);",
          "lang": "js"
        },
        {
          "id": "n8-md",
          "type": "md",
          "x": -265.87576067517557,
          "y": 669.1761506226218,
          "z": 12,
          "w": 340,
          "text": "A flow is simply an object made up of prompts. Run these prompts by calling the object with `ask()`."
        },
